<!-- ID: detailed_analysis -->
Why:
This review validated whether Forge Package 1.1 implemented only result-contract and mode-normalization work, without breaking existing callers or leaking Package 1.2+ scope.

What:
Checked the scoped diff for `runtime.py`, `scaffold_quality.py`, `quality/results.py`, `tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py`, and the active `CHECKLIST.md` proof line. Verified the required commands `pytest -q tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py` and `git diff --check`. Also ran a managed `quality_check` on the checklist proof.

How:
Evidence shows the runtime still returns the required top-level keys `ok`, `quality_status`, `scope`, `summary`, `warnings`, `runtime_warnings`, `readiness_blockers`, and `next_actions` in [runtime.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/runtime.py:1076). Default mode resolution falls back to `local_default` unless explicit `metadata.quality.mode == "release_gate"`, with explicit trigger attribution recorded in the summary only for that path in [runtime.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/runtime.py:884) and [runtime.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/runtime.py:1080). Warning normalization is centralized in [results.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/results.py:29), and deterministic ordering is defined by severity, code, then line in [results.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/results.py:40). The old summary helper was replaced by a compatibility import rather than a public action expansion in [scaffold_quality.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/scaffold_quality.py:8) and [scaffold_quality.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/scaffold_quality.py:183). Tests cover the preserved response keys, default `local_default` mode, non-blocking changelog coverage in ordinary context, and explicit `release_gate` trigger recording in [test_manage_docs_quality_check.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py:57), [test_manage_docs_quality_check.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py:261), and [test_manage_docs_quality_check.py](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py:300). The checklist proof item is present at [CHECKLIST.md](/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/quality_check_infrastructure_20260524/CHECKLIST.md:43), and the document itself currently passes managed `quality_check` in local-default mode with zero warnings/blockers.

Findings:
No blocking findings. Residual deduction only: the new ordering sorts severity lexicographically rather than by an explicit severity ranking, which is deterministic and documented in code, so it satisfies Package 1.1 but may deserve future refinement if consumers assume human-priority ordering.
